WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:01.979
Let me explain our student debt

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:04.139
forgiveness program to all of you.

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:05.849
You, the good people who are having

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:08.099
your loans forgiven, you people

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.779
who paid your loans or never got

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:11.099
them in the first place, and then

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:12.449
you people who never even went to

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:14.429
college. We're forgiving up to 20

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:15.929
grand of your student loan debt.

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:16.949
Yeah, because of our.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:17.819
Awesome.

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:20.039
Do not forget about us in November.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.569
Okay. I know you're mad.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:23.069
You struggled, you worked hard.

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:24.689
You missed a lot of opportunities to

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:26.159
get ahead in your professional

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:28.289
career, all to pay down your

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:30.839
debt responsibly, which proves

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:32.699
that you can do it again, for

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:33.779
them.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:35.699
Remember, this is targeted relief

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:37.619
for working class people,

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:39.719
like a married couple making 240

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:40.859
grand a year.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:42.419
You don't want them to suffer, do

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:43.420
you?

00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:48.079
Let me get back to you later.

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:50.059
Are you willing to donate just $7

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:51.499
to help us win in November?

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:52.999
We've got to keep making progress.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:54.589
Who knows? Maybe cancel some more

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:55.840
debt down the road, huh?

00:00:57.530 --> 00:00:59.419
No,  we can't stop subsidizing

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:00.379
student loans.

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:02.779
Harvard's endowment is only $50

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:04.009
billion.

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:05.779
You don't want Harvard to suffer, do

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:07.819
you? This really isn't about you.

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:09.619
So just chip in, do your part, but

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:10.519
stay out of the way.

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:11.689
Hey, can you believe they canceled

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:13.609
Samantha Bee? Like what?

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:14.929
What ratings problem?

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:16.579
Everyone I know watches that show.

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:17.749
The important thing is that we

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:19.729
mitigate the damage that we cause

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:21.289
without ever addressing the root

00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:22.639
cause of the problem.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:23.989
You don't want Congress to suffer,

00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:25.609
do you? Just put the money in the

00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:27.109
bucket and leave.

00:01:27.110 --> 00:01:28.249
No one wants to hear from you.

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:29.899
You just want people to suffer.

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:31.099
That's all we have to say.

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:32.809
Never engage with any substantive

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:34.759
argument or numbers or math

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:36.379
of any kind. It's only going to cost

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:38.539
about 300 billion or so

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:39.319
the first year.

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:40.849
We think with inflation, that's

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:42.219
going to feel like a lot less.

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:43.609
So if you guys were smart, you would

00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:44.539
have taken a loan you couldn't

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:45.889
afford to go to college, but you

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:47.239
didn't. So pony up.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.549
It's about two grand per taxpayer.

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:50.839
Put it in the bucket and leave.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:52.009
Do you guys want to get smoothies or

00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:53.569
something later? We need more people

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:54.679
in debt so they'll vote us into

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:56.629
office to get them out of debt.

00:01:56.630 --> 00:01:58.099
Thought you people went to college.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:01:59.359
Oh, please. You couldn't even spell

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:00.559
moral hazard.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:01.339
Cool.

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:02.269
Awesome.

00:02:02.270 --> 00:02:04.009
All right. November.

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:05.269
Of course it's constitutional

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:07.399
because of 9/11,

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:09.019
obviously.

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:10.159
Idiot.

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:12.049
Oh, I didn't see you there.

00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:13.849
You know, you kids are the future.

00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:15.079
That's why we're doing our best.

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:16.609
To make sure none of your actions

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:18.919
will ever have real consequences.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:20.689
Except maybe voting.

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:21.829
Well, you know, we're working on

00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:22.830
that, too.

